  "type": "multipleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A cylindrical capillary tube of <math><mn>0.2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> radius is made by joining two capillaries <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> of different materials having water contact angles of <math><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></math> and <math><msup><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></math> respectively. The capillary tube is dipped vertically in water in two different configurations, case I and II as shown in figure. Which of the following option(s) is(are) correct?<br >(Surface tension of water <math><mo>=</mo><mn>0.075</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></math> density of water <math><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></math> take <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></math><br ><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/qmseeagfrbqbbpolvlocklqjkhzvpshgqyojiasyhcbocthism.png\"/></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "0YOK8",
      "text": "For case II, if the capillary joint is  <math><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>  above the water surface, the height of water column raised in the tube will be  <math><mn>3.75</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>.</mo></math>  (Neglect the weight of the water in the meniscus)",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0ZH6l",
      "text": "For case I, if the joint is kept at  <math><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>  above the water surface, the height of water column in the tube will be  <math><mn>7.5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>.</mo></math>  (Neglect the weight of the water in the meniscus)",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "C6bRm",
      "text": "The correction in the height of water column raised in the tube, due to weight of water contained in the meniscus, will be different for both cases.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "T3kiS",
      "text": "For case I, if the capillary joint is  <math><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>  above the water surface, the height of water column raised in the tube will be more than  <math><mn>8.75</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>.</mo></math>  (Neglect the weight of the water in the meniscus)",
      "isCorrect": false,
