  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Heights if only single material tubes are used of sufficient length,\r\n\r\nFor table  <math><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mrow><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>0.075</mn><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>K</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1000</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>×</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>7.5</mn><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> \r\n\r\nFor table  <math><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mrow><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><msup><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>′</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>0.075</mn><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>60</mn><mo>°</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1000</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>×</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3.75</mn><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> \r\n\r\nWeight of water in meniscus will be different in two cases because angle of contact is different  <math><mo>⇒</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>  is correct.\r\n\r\nLiquid will rise only upto height of  <math><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>  and meniscus will adjust by changing is radius of curvature. If the liquid goes up in tube  <math><mn>2</mn></math>  then it will not be able to support the weight of the liquid  <math><mo>⇒</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>)</mo></math>  is incorrect.\r\n\r\nFor option  <math><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>)</mo></math>  Refer diagram below -\r\n\r\n <img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/srzppyajnsmxkbytwvuiqltfrgtukccqtwiusdozwratdimbdp.png\"/> \r\n\r\nAs  <math><msub><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math>  maximum height upto which liquid may rise in capillary is  <math><msub><mrow><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>7.5</mn><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> \r\n\r\nAnd length of tube available is  <math><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> \r\n\r\n <math><mo>⇒</mo></math>  Water will rise upto  <math><mn>7.5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> \r\n\r\n <math><mo>⇒</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>)</mo></math>  is correct.\r\n\r\nFor option  <math><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>)</mo></math> , Refer figure below -\r\n\r\n <img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/tugqiehtaukdwcdodipxhcqfknxqztkvndepmfddcqgjrppqow.png\"/> \r\n\r\nHere maximum height upto which water can rise in case- <math><mn>2</mn></math> ,  <math><msub><mrow><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3.75</mn><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> . Also the length of tube available is  <math><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> .\r\n\r\n <math><mo>⇒</mo></math>  Water will rise upto  <math><mn>3.75</mn><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> \r\n\r\n <math><mo>⇒</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>)</mo></math>  is correct.",
